# The body now

The torso is split into two segments: `Pelvis` (0.24 × 0.16, mass fraction 0.1117) and
`Torso` (0.24 × 0.34, fraction 0.3229). The pelvis-plus-chest sum 0.4346 is the former
fraction of the one-piece torso. Fractions are **not** normalized to 1: the neck `0.012` was added
on top of the full de Leva set, so the fraction sum is **1.012**, actual mass
**70.84 kg** at `totalMass = 70`. This is not a separate design of “neck above
norm”, but a bookkeeping consequence; do not change physics or fractions until there is a separate
mass task. Torque ceilings were still written for 70 kg.

Hips attach to the pelvis, neck and arms to the torso. Lumbar hinge ±20°, torque
90 N·m. The shoulder stays at the previous absolute height +0.125 via
`shoulderDropFromNeck`. Spawn point −0.82 was not changed.

**Knee flipped 24.08: limit `0…+120` instead of `−120…0`.** The former
range allowed only ostrich flexion. The `jointAngle` sign convention
and how to check it are in `balance-actuators.mdc`; here only the
consequence: knee flexion is now **plus**, hip flexion is still
minus, and that is not a typo but opposite sides of anatomy under one convention.

The intent layer (`MotionIntent`, `PlayerInputSource`) is wired to crouch and
walk (`StepPhaseDriver`, CLI `-walk`). All brains — `.cursor/rules/ai.mdc`.
Agent `ai` is currently bird AI (`BirdController.mode`), not the human.

