On all **survived** pushes the lumbar stays ≤ 9.58° of 20. It now
hits the stop only after `Falling`, i.e. as a consequence of the fall,
not as its cause. That was exactly the goal of the fix.

The landscape stopped being holey: `pelvisP` 1, 1.5, and 2 all stand
(`pelv_p1`, `pelv_p15`, `pelv_stand`); there are no neighboring “stands / falls”.

The knee was checked geometrically from the logs: it protrudes **+2.9 cm forward** of
the hip–ankle line instead of the former 4 cm back; the thigh is vertical, the foot
is flat.

Crouch became qualitatively different. Depth used to be limited by pelvis collapse: 5 cm
was reached with the pelvis at 36° and the lumbar at the stop. Now `crouch 1` gives 6.9 cm
at torso 2.15°, lumbar 17.3° without the stop, and the human returns to stance.

